{
  "readme": "# lkm4ctr\n\n`lkm4ctr` automatically loads `lkm4ctr.ko` to enable Docker and containers on all currently released arm64 Android GKI KMIs; no custom kernel flash. The module is intended for rooted devices and must match the device KMI exactly.\n\nSee [copying.txt](copying.txt) for the project and vendored-source license terms.\n\n## Start here\n\n1. Check the device kernel: `uname -a`\n2. Either download the matching `lkm4ctr-4.0.5-<kmi>-arm64.ko` release asset or install `lkm4ctr-kernelsu-module.zip` in KernelSU; the KernelSU module selects the matching KMI automatically\n3. Install `fuse-overlayfs` and configure Docker to use it by default (see the user manual)\n4. For a standalone `.ko` install, load it as root: `sudo insmod /path/to/lkm4ctr-4.0.5-<matching-kmi>-arm64.ko` (KernelSU installs and loads the bundled module itself)\n5. Start Docker: `sudo dockerd --config-file=\"$PREFIX/etc/docker/daemon.json\" --bridge=none --experimental`\n6. Test a container: `sudo docker run --network=host --rm -it docker.io/library/alpine:latest /bin/sh`\n\n`NET_NS` is currently bookkeeping-only, so host networking is required for network access. Read the manual before loading a module on a real device.\n\nThe KernelSU ZIP includes every KMI build and `lkm4ctr_checker`, enables boot auto-load by default, and provides an action button plus a multilingual WebUI for module control and checker output. Published releases include an update feed so KernelSU Manager can offer in-app updates when `versionCode` increases.\n\n## Documentation\n\n- [English user manual](docs/en/USER_GUIDE.md) · [简体中文](docs/zh-hans/USER_GUIDE.md) · [繁體中文](docs/zh-hant/USER_GUIDE.md)\n- [English architecture and developer documentation](docs/en/architecture/GLUE.md)\n- [English checker documentation](docs/en/developer/CHECKER.md)\n- [English vendor-kernel documentation](docs/en/developer/VENDOR_KERNEL.md)\n- [简体中文文档索引](docs/zh-hans/README.md) · [繁體中文文件索引](docs/zh-hant/README.md)\n\n`AGENTS.md` is the repository's contributor/agent contract and intentionally remains at the repository root.\n",
  "readmeHTML": "<h1>lkm4ctr</h1>\n\n<p><code>lkm4ctr</code> automatically loads <code>lkm4ctr.ko</code> to enable Docker and containers on all currently released arm64 Android GKI KMIs; no custom kernel flash. The module is intended for rooted devices and must match the device KMI exactly.</p>\n\n<p>See <a href=\"copying.txt\">copying.txt</a> for the project and vendored-source license terms.</p>\n\n<h2>Start here</h2>\n\n<li>Check the device kernel: `uname -a`</li>\n<li>Either download the matching `lkm4ctr-4.0.5-<kmi>-arm64.ko` release asset or install `lkm4ctr-kernelsu-module.zip` in KernelSU; the KernelSU module selects the matching KMI automatically</li>\n<li>Install `fuse-overlayfs` and configure Docker to use it by default (see the user manual)</li>\n<li>For a standalone `.ko` install, load it as root: `sudo insmod /path/to/lkm4ctr-4.0.5-<matching-kmi>-arm64.ko` (KernelSU installs and loads the bundled module itself)</li>\n<li>Start Docker: `sudo dockerd --config-file=\"$PREFIX/etc/docker/daemon.json\" --bridge=none --experimental`</li>\n<li>Test a container: `sudo docker run --network=host --rm -it docker.io/library/alpine:latest /bin/sh`</li>\n\n<p><code>NET_NS</code> is currently bookkeeping-only, so host networking is required for network access. Read the manual before loading a module on a real device.</p>\n\n<p>The KernelSU ZIP includes every KMI build and <code>lkm4ctr_checker</code>, enables boot auto-load by default, and provides an action button plus a multilingual WebUI for module control and checker output. Published releases include an update feed so KernelSU Manager can offer in-app updates when <code>versionCode</code> increases.</p>\n\n<h2>Documentation</h2>\n\n<li>[English user manual](docs/en/USER_GUIDE.md) · [简体中文](docs/zh-hans/USER_GUIDE.md) · [繁體中文](docs/zh-hant/USER_GUIDE.md)</li>\n<li>[English architecture and developer documentation](docs/en/architecture/GLUE.md)</li>\n<li>[English checker documentation](docs/en/developer/CHECKER.md)</li>\n<li>[English vendor-kernel documentation](docs/en/developer/VENDOR_KERNEL.md)</li>\n<li>[简体中文文档索引](docs/zh-hans/README.md) · [繁體中文文件索引](docs/zh-hant/README.md)</li>\n\n<p><code>AGENTS.md</code> is the repository's contributor/agent contract and intentionally remains at the repository root.</p>",
